## SQ-CIF-03 | Farmer's Respite coffee: Caffeinated plus a hidden Phantom Bane of the same length; rest stat not -24000; reset to 0 when it ends
> effect clear cb
> zc3 rest cb
> clear cb
> item replace entity cb weapon.mainhand with farmersrespite:coffee
> zp eat cb
waitlog \[zp\] done 20
> zp effects cb
waitlog \[zp\] effects cb: 20
expect effects cb: .*farmersrespite:caffeinated
expect effects cb: .*better_beacons:phantom_bane
capture PB better_beacons:phantom_bane amp \d+ (\d+)t
> zc3 rest cb
shell sleep $(( {PB} / 20 + 4 ))
> zp effects cb
> zc3 rest cb
waitlog \[c3\] done 20
reject rest cb: -2\d{4}
look Caffeinated and Phantom Bane durations equal; the rest stat after the drink is not near -24000; after Phantom Bane ends the stat reads near 0 (a few seconds of ticks, under about 200). If the coffee item id differs (farmersrespite:coffee is the cup), the eat line says so

## SQ-MIN-07 | fishing-net loot in a river and an ocean: biome-tagged entries (condition registered by Delight, no duplicate-id crash)
bootreject Duplicate.*biome_tag|already registered.*biome_tag
> locate biome minecraft:river
waitlog nearest minecraft:river is at|Could not find 300
capture RV minecraft:river is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> forceload add {RV1} {RV3}
> locate biome minecraft:ocean
waitlog nearest minecraft:ocean is at|Could not find 300
capture OC minecraft:ocean is at \[(-?\d+), (~|-?\d+), (-?\d+)\]
> forceload add {OC1} {OC3}
sleep 20
repeat 20
> loot spawn {RV1} 70 {RV3} loot creativedelight:gameplay/fishing_net/kelp
> loot spawn {OC1} 70 {OC3} loot creativedelight:gameplay/fishing_net/kelp
end
sleep 2
> execute positioned {RV1} 70 {RV3} run kill @e[type=minecraft:item,distance=..3]
> execute positioned {OC1} 70 {OC3} run kill @e[type=minecraft:item,distance=..3]
> forceload remove {RV1} {RV3}
> forceload remove {OC1} {OC3}
reject Couldn't parse loot table|Unknown loot table|biome_tag.*(not registered|Unknown)
look the `loot spawn` reply lines ("Dropped N items" or the item list) differ between river and ocean per the table's biome_tag conditions (read the table creativedelight:gameplay/fishing_net/kelp.json for which tag gates which entry); in-game net fishing itself is a client check. Also check sea_grass if kelp has no biome entries

